She heard commotion at her back and before she could even turn her head, a chest collided with hers—the comforting scent of cedar filling her nose as she was pulled into Theo’s arms. He squeezed her tight and for some reason Hermione couldn’t explain, she clung to him, her heart thundering with a sadness that shouldn’t belong. Theo felt it and pulled back, looking at her with furrowed brows.

